/ A row of the table from lg up: the icon, the place with its locality, the
  cars, the visits and the latest visit. Below lg a cell of a grouped list:
  the icon, the place in the first line, and its cars with the visits at the
  right in the second. The place takes the whole width up to the chevron.
= render Ui::TableRow::Component.new(href:, nav_title: t('settings.places.edit'), css_class: 'grid items-center lg:col-span-full lg:grid-cols-subgrid max-lg:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)_auto_auto] max-lg:grid-rows-[auto_auto] max-lg:gap-y-0.5') do |row|
  .lg:p-2.max-lg:row-span-2
    = render Place::Icon::Component.new(place:)
  .min-w-0.lg:p-2.max-lg:col-span-2.max-lg:col-start-2.max-lg:row-start-1
    = row.link css_class: 'block truncate text-fg' do
      = render Place::VisitList::NameCell::Component.new(place:)
      = render Place::VisitList::LocalityCell::Component.new(place:)
  / Each car in its color, like in the list of the charging sessions
  .min-w-0.flex.gap-1.lg:flex-wrap.lg:p-2.max-lg:overflow-hidden.max-lg:col-start-2.max-lg:row-start-2
    - cars.each do |car|
      = render Car::Badge::Component.new(car:, short: true)
  / The number of visits as a short "24 ×". Its full name is its label for
    screen readers.
    The visits are a target of their own on the desktop, like the day of a
    charging session. On a phone a tap opens the place, whose page leads to
    them.
  .tabular-nums.text-right.whitespace-nowrap.font-semibold.text-fg.lg:p-2.max-lg:col-start-3.max-lg:row-start-2.max-lg:font-normal.max-lg:text-subhead.max-lg:text-fg-secondary
    = link_to t('.visits', count: visit_count), visits_href, 'aria-label': t('visits.count', count: visit_count), class: 'max-lg:pointer-events-none rounded-sm lg:hover:underline underline-offset-4 focus-ring-inset'
  .hidden.lg:block.tabular-nums.text-right.whitespace-nowrap.text-fg-secondary.p-2
    = t('.last', date: last)
